{"section":{"id":"cet4-2026-06-set1-passage-2","examId":"cet4-2026-06-set1","title":"短文 2","kind":"短文","start":1048.19,"end":1153.23,"preview":"Plastics have for years been used to make nearly everything that surrounds us.","lines":[{"start":1048.19,"end":1053.71,"text":"Plastics have for years been used to make nearly everything that surrounds us."},{"start":1053.71,"end":1063.47,"text":"But along the way, they escaped the confines of packaging and objects and settled in the environment, the food we eat, and the air we breathe."},{"start":1063.47,"end":1067.78,"text":"Americans are consuming and breathing in a lot of plastic."},{"start":1067.78,"end":1079.47,"text":"Based on available data, Americans take in an estimated 74,000 to 121,000 microplastic particles every year."},{"start":1079.47,"end":1088.83,"text":"Scientists believe the true number is probably much higher, because for some likely sources of microplastics, there was no strong data available."},{"start":1088.83,"end":1093.47,"text":"Microplastics get into food and air in several ways."},{"start":1093.47,"end":1106.11,"text":"Many start off as part of larger plastic objects, which over time fragment into smaller and smaller pieces, until they become tiny, 5mm or less in diameter."},{"start":1106.11,"end":1111.31,"text":"They are breathed in or consumed by animals that then become our food."},{"start":1111.31,"end":1115.87,"text":"The particles float through the air until people breathe them in."},{"start":1115.87,"end":1119.39,"text":"They also settle on the food that people eat."},{"start":1119.39,"end":1129.23,"text":"Data shows that for Americans, air, bottled water and seafood were the biggest sources for breathed in or consumed microplastics."},{"start":1129.23,"end":1137.55,"text":"Added sugars accounted for less, and salts, tap water, and beer contributed minimal amounts."},{"start":1137.55,"end":1140.11,"text":"These estimates are conservative."},{"start":1140.11,"end":1145.78,"text":"The included foods only make up about 15% of the average American diet."},{"start":1145.78,"end":1153.23,"text":"It's not yet known how much plastic is contained in the remaining 85% of the typical diet."}],"audio":"assets/audio/5c22a4391ab2d904965fd012646fa9336fda2c80dba184ef6282056a0d3e1479.wav","audioOffset":1048.19},"tasks":[{"id":"0-0","text":"Plastics have for years been used to make nearly everything that surrounds us.","start":1048.19,"end":1053.71,"legacyTaskIds":["0-0"],"legacyTaskIndices":[0],"sentenceVisual":{"type":"事件","icon":"shapes","image":"assets/images/8d1559716246b37ad1062b4ee71ae87fb0392e432a499cd71e75a7db67e6f1e5.webp","alt":"塑料构成许多日常用品的情境"},"chunks":[{"text":"Plastics have for years been used to make nearly everything that surrounds us.","start":1048.19,"end":1053.71,"visual":{"type":"事件","icon":"shapes","image":"assets/images/8d1559716246b37ad1062b4ee71ae87fb0392e432a499cd71e75a7db67e6f1e5.webp","alt":"塑料构成许多日常用品的情境"}}],"variants":{"overview":[{"text":"Plastics have for years been used to make nearly everything that surrounds us.","start":1048.19,"end":1053.71,"visual":{"type":"事件","icon":"shapes","image":"assets/images/8d1559716246b37ad1062b4ee71ae87fb0392e432a499cd71e75a7db67e6f1e5.webp","alt":"塑料构成许多日常用品的情境"}}],"standard":[{"text":"Plastics have for years been used to make nearly everything that surrounds us.","start":1048.19,"end":1053.71,"visual":{"type":"事件","icon":"shapes","image":"assets/images/8d1559716246b37ad1062b4ee71ae87fb0392e432a499cd71e75a7db67e6f1e5.webp","alt":"塑料构成许多日常用品的情境"}}],"fine":[{"text":"Plastics","start":1048.19,"end":1048.79,"visual":{"type":"事件","icon":"shapes","image":"assets/images/56eeca3474d264d5d44a9d65038baf83a27bf70da6103fad8ed9028b024508a1.webp","alt":"常见塑料物品"}},{"text":"have for years been used to make nearly everything that surrounds us.","start":1048.79,"end":1053.71,"visual":{"type":"事件","icon":"shapes","image":"assets/images/32d19c223f4db9d7dabff37adac1e511b204d5991fd2aefb05e383277ff99316.webp","alt":"人们使用塑料制成